course: dictionary
lesson: 11106
title: A whim
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A whim is a sudden wish or idea to do something, often without a good reason. Look at the words around it to find its meaning. «A piggy bank that is hard to open helps you save, because getting money out takes effort, so you do not spend it on a whim.» The words "so you do not spend" tell you that spending on a whim means spending quickly, without planning.
explain: The second sentence gives the same idea in fewer words: «A piggy bank that is hard to open makes it harder to spend savings on a whim.» Swap in your meaning to check it: "harder to spend savings on a sudden wish" still makes sense, so whim means a sudden wish.
explain: Whim is a noun, so you can have a whim or several whims. Phrases like "on a whim" mean suddenly, without planning, and "a passing whim" is a wish that does not last long.
fact: A whim is a sudden wish or idea, often without a good reason.
fact: «On a whim» means suddenly, without planning.
fact: «A passing whim» is a wish that does not last long.
fact: A piggy bank that is hard to open helps you save, because you think before you take money out.
fact: Context clues, such as "so you do not spend", can help you work out what a word means.
exercise: «A piggy bank that is hard to open makes it harder to spend savings on a whim.» What is a whim? | A kind of piggy bank | A heavy coin | *A sudden wish or idea with no planning behind it | A careful plan made for months
exercise: Mum says, «We are going to the beach on a whim!» What does on a whim mean? | After many weeks of careful planning | *Suddenly, without planning | Very slowly | Only if it rains
exercise: Which word means a sudden wish? «She bought a new kite on a whim.» | kite | new | bought | *whim
test: Why does a hard-to-open piggy bank help you save? | Because it is made of gold | Because it is shiny and fun to look at | *Because you have to think before you take money out | Because it holds more money than a bag
test: Which phrase means a wish that does not last long? | A careful plan | *A passing whim | A sad story | A long journey
exam: Which sentence uses whim correctly? | The whim was very tall and green | He read the whim on the map | *She changed her mind about the trip on a whim | We whim the table yesterday
